{
  "_notes": [
    "Runtime zoning-district lookup. Each entry points at a jurisdiction's own published",
    "GIS layer -- the only place zoning actually lives, since it is a per-municipality legal",
    "designation and no global geocoder (Google included) carries it.",
    "",
    "district_categories maps the layer's raw zoning code to the coarse vocabulary the source",
    "packs are tagged with. Every mapping is derived from that city's OWN ordinance or from the",
    "layer's own published district name -- never guessed. scripts/derive_gis_district_categories.py",
    "regenerates them and writes the evidence sentence behind each one; run it after a rescrape.",
    "A code absent from this map yields a parcel id but no district, which is the same position",
    "we were in before the lookup existed -- never a guess.",
    "",
    "jurisdiction_field/jurisdiction_value guard against a geocode landing on a neighbouring",
    "parcel outside the town limits: a shared county layer serves several jurisdictions, so a row",
    "whose jurisdiction_field does not match is discarded rather than answered with. A layer that",
    "only ever covers one jurisdiction omits both keys."
  ],
